detector_raw:
{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this packing plan — are you trying to minimize the number of containers used, maximize the total weight (or units) of goods shipped, or something else?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting mutually exclusive options for one decision."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since you want to pack all the goods, does every available unit of each type (A, B, C, D, E) have to be loaded into containers, or is it acceptable to leave some units unshipped if that lets you use fewer containers?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether all units must be shipped or if some can be left unshipped to minimize container count."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "is the real goal to ship as much total weight (or as many total units) of goods as possible, subject to using the minimum number of containers needed to carry that amount?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the optimization objective (maximize shipment subject to minimum containers)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "does the \"at least 12 units of type D\" rule apply to every container that is used, or only to containers that actually contain some type D goods?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a specific policy scope choice."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Does this apply to every container that is used (i.e., if a container has even one unit of A, it must have at least one unit of C), or is there a different reading you had in mind?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single clarification regarding the interpretation of the rule, presenting two mutually exclusive options for the same policy constraint."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is it acceptable for some D units to be left unshipped (e.g., 6 units if 7 containers are used), or must all 90 D units be loaded?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy decision regarding whether unused D units are permitted or if full utilization is mandatory."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any rule about what happens to a container that ends up below 18 tons — for example, must such a container simply not be used (i.e., it is not counted and its goods must be redistributed), or is there a penalty or other treatment?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the treatment of containers below the 18-ton minimum, presenting mutually exclusive options within one semantic query."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the goods of each type divisible (so a container could hold, say, 12.5 units of A), or must the number of units of each type in each container be a whole number?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the divisibility of goods, presenting two mutually exclusive options for the same constraint."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is 60 tons a hard upper limit that no container may exceed, or is it just a nominal capacity where slightly exceeding it would be acceptable?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the nature of the 60-ton limit (hard vs. nominal), which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "is there any limit on the total number of containers you can use, or is the only constraint the per-container weight and composition rules?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking whether the constraint is a total count limit or only per-container rules. The first sentence is explanatory context, not a question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say \"pack all the goods,\" does that mean the plan must ship every available unit of every type (A: 120, B: 90, C: 300, D: 90, E: 120), or is it acceptable to leave some units unshipped as long as the per-type totals don't exceed availability?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding whether 'pack all' implies shipping 100% of available inventory or allows for partial shipment within availability limits. This is a single binary choice."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any rule about how the goods of different types can be combined within a single container — for example, can a container hold any mix of A, B, C, D, E in any proportions (subject to the stated rules), or are there additional restrictions on which types can share a container?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the rules for combining different goods types within a container."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any other business rules or constraints I should know about that aren't covered by the weight limits, the D minimum, the A-requires-C rule, and the per-type availability caps?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking if there are additional constraints beyond the listed ones."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "whether the number of units per container must be a whole number",
    "whether there is a fixed fleet size of containers available"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for confirmation on two distinct constraints: the integrality of units per container and the fixedness of the fleet size. These are independent facts that can be answered separately."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Given that multiple key points are still pending internal confirmation, would you like me to proceed with modeling based on the confirmed constraints (per-container weight 18–60 tons, at least 12 D units per used container, A implies at least 1 C, per-type availability caps) and the stated goal of minimizing containers, treating the unresolved items (exact objective, integrality, whether all goods must ship) as assumptions I will flag in the model?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single compound question asking for permission to proceed with specific assumptions. Although it lists multiple items, they are all part of one decision request (whether to proceed with the proposed approach), so it counts as one independent question."
}
